---
description: Astro architecture, TypeScript, Tailwind and deployment conventions
globs: '**/*.{astro,ts,tsx,js,mjs,css,json}'
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture.md`.

- Astro static generation is the default; avoid client-side hydration unless justified.
- Use existing `BaseLayout` and established site components/styles.
- Tailwind CSS 4 is configured through `@tailwindcss/vite`; do not reintroduce the obsolete Astro Tailwind integration.
- Keep dependencies minimal. No React, CMS, database or dedicated backend without approval.
- Contact form server functionality should be compatible with Cloudflare Pages Functions or the chosen Cloudflare deployment model. Verify the deployment model before adding endpoint code.
- Never place secrets in `public/`, client JavaScript or `PUBLIC_` environment variables.
- Preserve Astro 7 compatibility; verify actual versions in `package.json`.
